      "alt": "rinmeetsthehole4"
    },
    {
      "en": ""
    },
    {
      "en": ": Haven’t they like totally not been doing anything though lol.",
      "spk": "Chika",
      "spkColor": "#AF7F00",
      "zh": ""
    },
    {
      "en": ": WHY DON’T YOU JUST STAY BROKEN? I LIKE YOU BETTER THAT WAY AND YOU’LL HAVE MORE MONEY TO SPEND ON MONK.",
      "spk": "Chika",
      "spkColor": "#AF7F00",
      "zh": ""
    },
    {
      "en": ": Buy more monk. Eat more monk. Chop more monk. Monk, monk, monk!",
      "spk": "Sensei",
      "spkColor": "#969696",
      "zh": ""
    },
    {
      "en": ": GET THE FUCK AWAY FROM ME!!!",
      "spk": "Rin",
      "spkColor": "#FF00AE",
      "zh": ""
    },
    {
      "en": ""
    },
    {
      "en": "scene black",
      "cap": true,
      "zh": ""
    },
    {
      "img": "游戏图片/Misc/black.png",
      "alt": "black"
    },
    {
      "en": ""
    },
    {
      "en": "Rin never ate the spaghetti. Probably because there wasn’t any spaghetti at all. And it’s hard to eat things that aren’t there.",
      "zh": ""
    },
    {
      "en": "This doesn’t stop everyone, though. And sometimes, people create the foods they want to eat out of thin air because they have weirdly specific superpowers that let them sacrifice laymen for nutrients.",
      "zh": ""
    },
    {
      "en": "One of those laymen was my mother. I keep her voice in a bottle in the corner of my room, next to letters about footsteps and memories of holidays that are now spaghetti too.",
      "zh": ""
    },
    {
      "en": "I am so very sad.",
      "zh": ""
    },
    {
      "en": "Let us be sad together for the next ten seconds.",
      "zh": ""
    },
    {
      "en": ""
    },
    {
      "en": ""
    },
    {
      "en": "I bet you’re probably thinking that was longer than ten seconds. And in thinking that, you’d be right.",
      "zh": ""
    },
    {
      "en": "Because there are only some places where the flow of time changes. And we currently exist in the space between yes and no, where that truth isn’t as much of a truth as it is a memory.",
      "zh": ""
    },
    {
      "en": "But that’s something that gets lost in translation sometimes.",
      "zh": ""
    },
    {
      "en": "Maybe we’re just bad at counting. Maybe we do it for the attention. But whatever reasons we do it for doesn’t change the fact that we do it.",
      "zh": ""
    },
    {
      "en": "That we’re still doing it.",
      "zh": ""
    },
    {
      "en": "And when we’re not, we’re thinking about doing it.",
      "zh": ""
    },
    {
      "en": "Then when we’re doing it, we’re thinking about doing it again.",
      "zh": ""
    },
    {
      "en": "Over and over and over until the gods that govern our sadness grow ten times fatter and a hundred times stronger than we can.",
      "zh": ""
    },
    {
      "en": "It all goes unseen and unsolved.",
      "zh": ""
    },
    {
      "en": "We haven’t made it to ten yet.",
      "zh": ""
    },
    {
      "en": ""
    },
    {
